  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.CastRay(Start: vector, End: vector, Options: {any}): {any}`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`list llCastRay(vector Start, vector End, list Options);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Cast a line from <b>start</b> to <b>end</b> and report collision data for intersections with objects.</p>
  <p>Returns a list of strided values on a successful hit, with an additional integer <a href="#status_code" target="_blank">status_code</a> at the end.</p>
  <p>Each stride consists of two mandatory values &#123;<a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Key" target="_blank">key</a> <b>uuid</b>, <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Vector" target="_blank">vector</a> <b>position</b>&#125; and optionally &#123;<a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Integer" target="_blank">integer</a> <b>link_number</b>, <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Vector" target="_blank">vector</a> <b>normal</b>&#125;. (See <a href="#RC_DATA_FLAGS" target="_blank">RC_DATA_FLAGS</a> for details.)</p>
  <p>A negative <b>status_code</b> is an <a href="#error_code" target="_blank">error code</a>, otherwise it is the number of hits (and strides) returned.</p>
</p>
